NEW and deletion locks the row at the generation it claimed, so a host that reconnects mid-sweep wins. ## A paid T3 Chat plan raises the tunnel cap T3 Chat uses WorkOS, not Clerk, so the two accounts are linked by consent rather than by a shared identity. The relay and T3 Chat share one secret (`T3CHAT_LINK_SECRET` here, `T3CODE_LINK_SECRET` there). The relay signs a short-lived token naming the Clerk user and email; the user confirms it while signed in to T3 Chat, and T3 Chat stores the link. T3 Chat owns the link and the plan, so the relay keeps no copy. It asks T3 Chat only when an account reaches its normal cap for a new environment, and any failure keeps the normal cap. An environment that already holds a counted slot restarts without asking, so a downgrade or a T3 Chat outage only blocks new environments. A manual override row replaces the default for new environments, and a T3 Chat plan does not raise it ([limits](../../infra/relay/src/environments/ManagedTunnelLimits.ts)). ## The relay client follows the server's pin The host runs `cloudflared` pinned by `CLOUDFLARED_VERSION` in [`relayClient.ts`](../../packages/shared/src/relayClient.ts), and bumping it there (version, URLs, and checksums) is the whole release step. A linked host that starts a server with a new pin keeps its connector up on the newest older managed release, installs the pinned one in the background, then starts a second connector on it for the same tunnel. The old connector stops only after the new one registers, so the swap never takes the host off the relay. If the new one fails to spawn, the old one keeps serving and the install retries later. A host with no relay client installs one first. A `cloudflared` on `PATH` or an explicit `T3CODE_CLOUDFLARED_PATH` is the user's choice and is never replaced, since linking asks before downloading. Once the pinned release registers a connection, managed releases older than the pin are deleted except the newest of them. That one, and any newer release, can belong to another server sharing the same T3 home, such as a rollback after a failed update, which could not run again without it. The version comes from running `cloudflared version`, not from the folder name. Connectors from before `--no-autoupdate` replaced themselves in place, so a managed folder can hold another release. Such a binary still runs as a fallback while the pin installs. Every binary needs `CLOUDFLARED_MIN_VERSION`, the oldest release that accepts every flag the connector is started with. Raise it whenever a new flag is added. ## OAuth traps Interactive clients and the headless CLI use the same Clerk application but different credentials. The relay
